export const ROD = {
"quest.q1.offer.1": "Warden Ilse. Welcome to {town}. If you're looking for work, I've got wolves taking sheep right outside the gate.",
"quest.q1.offer.2": "One chased the baker up the main street last night. Kill eight before they decide the rest of us are food.",
"quest.q1.turnin.1": "Eight? Good. I'll tell the shepherds they can use the near pasture again. Come back when you've had more practice. There's worse out there.",
"quest.q2.offer.1": "Bram. Mind that hide, it's wet. I'm trying to get everyone's winter boots finished before their toes freeze off.",
"quest.q2.offer.2": "I need six pelts. Wolf or bear will do. And aim away from the belly, will you? That's the bit I can sell.",
"quest.q2.turnin.1": "Let me see. Yes, I can use these. You've left me enough hide to work with.",
"quest.q3.offer.1": "No merchants into {town} today. Brigands have camps all along the Kingsroad, and word's got around.",
"quest.q3.offer.2": "Take a group and kill ten. Watch for anything that tells us who's paying them. Somebody's keeping those camps supplied.",
"quest.q3.turnin.1": "I'll send word that the road's open. With luck, we can get a few wagons through before they regroup.",
"quest.q4.offer.1": "Their captain's called {captain}. Eastern camp. He lets his crew do the fighting until things go badly enough to drag him out.",
"quest.q4.offer.2": "Hit the crew. When he comes out, finish him. I need proof before I can close the bounty.",
"quest.q4.turnin.1": "{captain}. That's him. Here's your bounty. You've earned every copper.",
"quest.q5.offer.1": "A Tusk warband's come out of the southern wood. War paint, torches, the lot. I'm not waiting for them to reach my drying racks.",
"quest.q5.offer.2": "Kill the bonecallers first. They heal the brutes while you're fighting them. Leave one singing and you'll have to do the whole job twice.",
"quest.q5.turnin.1": "Broken them up, have you? Good. Maybe I can get someone back into the wood for bark. Here's what I owe you.",
"quest.q6.offer.1": "The war dead still walk the Grey Waste. Usually they keep to the ruins. Something has stirred them up.",
"quest.q6.offer.2": "Put twelve to rest, {hero}. Say a few words over them if you have time. They had names once.",
"quest.q6.turnin.1": "Thank you. I'll light candles for them tonight.",
"quest.q7.offer.1": "There's a troll in the hollow at the far end of the southern wood. The orcs call him {tusk}. Even the warband gives him room.",
"quest.q7.offer.2": "I've sent hunters after him. None came back. If you go, take a full group and a healer who can keep their head.",
"quest.q7.turnin.1": "{tusk} is dead? You're certain? I need to tell the hunters' families. They've been waiting a long time.",
"quest.q8.offer.1": "The bodies are going to the Ossuary. Corwin said so, and the letter confirms it.",
"quest.q8.offer.2": "Take a full group, {hero}. Clear the court and the great hall, then find out what the Choir is building. Those ruins were sealed under the Fourfold Law for a reason.",
"quest.q8.turnin.1": "You've cleared both? Then the crypt is all that's left. I wish I could tell you to go home and rest.",
"quest.q8.turnin.2": "Can you go back in?",
"quest.q9.offer.1": "Corwin gave me a name: Grathul. The Gravelord stitched it together from soldiers killed in the war. It's still down in the Ossuary's crypt.",
"quest.q9.offer.2": "Destroy it before the Choir can finish their work. Take six of your best, including a healer you trust.",
"quest.q9.turnin.1": "You saw the Gravelord? After Grathul fell? Tell me exactly what you saw.",
"quest.q9.turnin.2": "A hundred years. We've been teaching children that he was dead. Give me a moment, {hero}. Please.",
"quest.m1.offer.1": "You! You've got a weapon. Could you come here a moment? I'm Wick. I dig the graves for {town}. Something's happened.",
"quest.m1.offer.2": "Three graves were open this morning. Mother Abernathy's, the Cobb twins', and my Uncle Bartholomew's. I filled them myself. They were shut when I left.",
"quest.m1.offer.3": "Will you look? I got as far as the edge, but then some dirt moved. Probably just dirt. I'd still rather you looked.",
"quest.m1.turnin.1": "From the inside? They dug out from the inside? I was hoping you'd say foxes.",
"quest.m1.turnin.2": "What do I tell their families? I can't very well say I've lost them.",
"quest.m2.offer.1": "There are tracks past the north fields. Long furrows through the grass, like someone's dragged something heavy. They weren't there yesterday.",
"quest.m2.offer.2": "Can you follow them? I'll stay here in case anyone else comes up. Comes back. You know what I mean.",
"quest.m2.turnin.1": "The Ossuary. Right. Of course they couldn't have gone somewhere we could just knock.",
"quest.m2.turnin.2": "We need the Watch. I'll keep the families away from the graves until we know what to tell them.",
"quest.m3.offer.1": "Could you tell Warden Ilse? She'll listen to you. She still brings up the cat whenever I go near the Watch house.",
"quest.m3.offer.2": "I buried her cat last spring. Except it wasn't hers. Hers came home the next morning. I thought she'd be pleased.",
"quest.m3.turnin.1": "Graves opened from below, tracks toward the Ossuary. You saw this yourself? Good. I need more than Wick's account.",
"quest.m3.turnin.2": "I believe you. Somebody's moving our dead, and they've done it right under the Watch's nose. Let's find out who.",
"quest.m4.offer.1": "The Kingsroad brigands have been taking odd jobs lately. If someone's hiring grave robbers, they'd know.",
"quest.m4.offer.2": "Search their camps east and west of town. Look for digging tools, anything with graveyard soil on it. Bring me something I can use.",
"quest.m4.turnin.1": "Grave mud. Same as Abernathy's plot. So they had people digging from above as well. Now we need to find out who paid them.",
"quest.m5.offer.1": "Check the diggers' purses. Whoever hired them had to pay, and I want to see the money.",
"quest.m5.offer.2": "Take the coins to Sister Maren at the temple. She knows the old currencies better than I do.",
"quest.m5.turnin.1 [sister]": "Bone coin. Set it down, please. The Pale Choir used these to pay men to dig up the battlefields.",
"quest.m5.turnin.2 [sister]": "They sang while the Gravelord raised the bodies. His faithful. We were told the last of them died a hundred years ago. Where did you find these?",
"quest.m6.offer.1": "Scouts saw pale robes west of the Kingsroad, beyond the brigand camp on the road to Little Hollin. Close enough to reach our graves after dark.",
"quest.m6.offer.2": "Break up their camp and bring me any papers you find. Be careful, {hero}. They believe this work is sacred. They won't surrender easily.",
"quest.m6.turnin.1": "Little Hollin. Here, again, in the next hymn. They say the dead are already rising there. Mayor Pell has been writing to me about ghosts for weeks.",
"quest.m6.turnin.2": "I put his letters in a drawer. I'll write an apology. Will you go and help him?",
"quest.m7.offer.1": "Take the west road past the Choir camp. Little Hollin's about an hour away. You can't miss the turnip fields.",
"quest.m7.offer.2": "Find Mayor Pell. Tell him I've read his letters, and that I'm sorry it took this long.",
"quest.m7.turnin.1 [pell]": "Welcome to Hollin! Mind the... yes, that's a ghost. We've had rather a week. Please don't leave.",
"quest.m7.turnin.2 [pell]": "Dobbin Pell, mayor. Maren sent you? At last. Come in. I'll find you a chair Mrs. Gubbins hasn't moved.",
"quest.m8.offer.1": "A fellow called Brother Ansel has moved into the chapel yard. Rings the bell at midnight, every night. That's when the voices start in the graves.",
"quest.m8.offer.2": "I asked him to leave. He hissed at me. In my own chapel yard! Perhaps you could be more persuasive.",
"quest.m8.turnin.1 [ansel]": "Stop! I yield! Please. I rang the bell. That's all I did. They said it would bring my brother back.",
"quest.m8.turnin.2 [ansel]": "He never came. All those other people, and never him. I wanted to stop, but the Deacon checks. He'd have known.",
"quest.m8.turnin.3 [ansel]": "Mortlake. Deacon Mortlake, in the Grey Waste. He sends the bodies north to the Ossuary. For the Gravelord, he says. I didn't ask any more.",
"quest.m9.offer.1": "The Gravelord? Ansel actually said that? My mother used to sing those songs to frighten us into bed.",
"quest.m9.offer.2": "Go straight to Sister Maren in {town}. I'll get everyone indoors. I know a bolt won't stop a ghost, but I have to do something.",
"quest.m9.turnin.1 [sister]": "The Gravelord died at the Ossuary. That's what every history says. The four courts broke his armies there at the end of the wars.",
"quest.m9.turnin.2 [sister]": "None of them says who found his body.",
"quest.m9.turnin.3 [sister]": "Corwin Ashlar fought him. He lives in a tower at the western edge of the Grey Waste. If anyone knows what really happened, it's Corwin. Getting him to talk will be another matter.",
"quest.m10.offer.1": "Corwin was barely grown when he fought the necromancers. He's had a hundred years to get tired of questions. I send him jam at the solstice to keep us on speaking terms.",
"quest.m10.offer.2": "His tower's past the harpy crag, at the western edge of the Waste. Be patient with him. And watch what he has in his hands when you knock.",
"quest.m10.turnin.1 [corwin]": "No. Whatever it is, no.",
"quest.m10.turnin.2 [corwin]": "Maren sent you. I can tell. She always sends the persistent ones. Did she at least send jam?",
"quest.m10.turnin.3 [corwin]": "Come in, then. Boots on the mat. I'm a hundred and twenty; don't waste the afternoon getting to the point.",
"quest.m11.offer.1": "Pale robes outside my tower for a month. They creep past the windows as if I don't know what they are.",
"quest.m11.offer.2": "Get rid of them. Then we'll talk about the Gravelord. I'm not giving the Choir a seat at the table.",
"quest.m11.turnin.1": "They've stopped humming. Thank you. I was beginning to hear it in my sleep.",
"quest.m11.turnin.2": "Take the stool. Not that chair, it bites. Now. What has Maren told you?",
"quest.m12.turnin.1": "Give me the letter. Hold the lamp closer.",
"quest.m12.turnin.2": "The little skulls over the i's. Yes. That's his handwriting.",
"quest.m12.turnin.3": "He's alive, {hero}. Whatever that word means for him. And all this time, I've been sitting here.",
"quest.m13.offer.1": "Before you go, there's something I need to tell you. Sit down.",
"quest.m13.offer.2": "You haven't asked how I know his rituals. Most people don't. It's one reason I chose a tower so far from town.",
"quest.m13.turnin.1": "I won't ask you to forgive it. You weren't there. You aren't the person I need to ask.",
"quest.m13.turnin.2": "If you still want my help, you have it. If you want to leave, I won't stop you.",
"quest.m16.offer.1": "An ocean of dead. He means the Saltreach. All those warships went down off the coast with their crews aboard.",
"quest.m16.offer.2": "Follow the Kingsroad east, {hero}. Find Harbormaster Quell in Saltmarrow and explain what's coming. Take Wick if he'll go. He's already packed.",
"quest.m16.offer.3 [wick]": "Three shovels. Is that too many? I've never been to the sea. I don't know what the ground's like.",
"quest.m16.turnin.1 [quell]": "Walking dead? Fourth report this week. Where did you see them?",
"quest.m16.turnin.2 [quell]": "You killed the Stitched Thing? In the Ossuary? Come inside. Start there, and leave nothing out.",
"quest.h1.offer.1": "Most of the ghosts are harmless. Mrs. Gubbins moves my chairs around every night. I've given up moving them back.",
"quest.h1.offer.2": "The ones in the fields are attacking people. Can you deal with them? I knew some of them. Please be as gentle as you can.",
"quest.h1.turnin.1": "I can hear the sheep again. Never thought I'd miss that noise. Thank you.",
"quest.h2.offer.1": "Hold this thread. No, the other end. Half the village needs charm bags for their windows, and I've run out of silk.",
"quest.h2.offer.2": "Six strands from the big spiders south of here. Check for eggs before you bring them into my house.",
"quest.h2.turnin.1": "Good. Hold the bag open while I put this away. Your pay's on the table.",
"quest.h3.offer.1": "Haskett's still at the mill. Every night, grinding away. He died last spring. None of us knows quite how to bring it up.",
"quest.h3.offer.2": "Would you speak to him? He might listen to a stranger. Whenever I visit, he wants to discuss my flour bill.",
"quest.h3.turnin.1 [haskett]": "Customer! About time. Copper a sack. You brought a sack, I hope? My hands go through the string.",
"quest.h3.turnin.2 [haskett]": "Pell sent you to tell me I'm dead, didn't he? Look at me. I know. Ask him when he's planning to pay for his flour.",
"quest.h4.offer.1": "Grumblesnout. Huge boar, west fields. Ate my prize turnips the day I died. I went out to chase him off, and... well. Here we are.",
"quest.h4.offer.2": "Bring me his tusk. I'd like to have a look at him from this end for a change.",
"quest.h4.turnin.1": "That's it. That's the one. Set it on the shelf where I can see it. Ha. Let's see him eat a turnip now.",
"quest.h5.offer.1": "Maren knows a rite to send me on. I've been thinking about asking her. The nights are long when you don't sleep.",
"quest.h5.offer.2": "But the mill needs someone. I could stay, keep it turning through winter. Hollin would have bread. What would you do?",
"quest.h5.turnin.1": "Well? I'm listening.",
"quest.h6.offer.1": "There are three warding bells around Hollin. We rang them every dusk for two hundred years. Kept the dead where we put them.",
"quest.h6.offer.2": "The bell-ringer died. Nobody took over. Go ring all three, and keep your weapon handy. They'll draw more than complaints.",
"quest.h6.turnin.1": "There. I can take the salt off my windowsill tonight. I'll find someone to keep the bells going.",
"quest.h7.offer.1": "Ansel's friends are still at the chapel. I can hear them singing from my bedroom.",
"quest.h7.offer.2": "Clear them out, please. People need somewhere to marry and bury their dead. Especially now.",
"quest.h7.turnin.1": "We can use the chapel again. I'll tell everyone. Mrs. Gubbins has already started on the pews, so I think she approves.",
"quest.h8.offer.1": "Get me some of those grey hymnbooks. I want to know what they're singing before I burn the lot.",
"quest.h8.offer.2": "Four should do. Take ones they've used. The notes in the margins might tell us more than the hymns.",
"quest.h8.turnin.1": "'We sing so that they may rise.' Hm. This one has names beside the verses. And dates.",
"quest.h8.turnin.2": "Here's the Ossuary again. And a Deacon. Maren needs to see these before they go in the fire. Your pay's there.",
"quest.h9.offer.1": "Venn's still at the old shrine east of the village. The Choirmaster. As long as he's there, they'll keep coming back.",
"quest.h9.offer.2": "Please stop him, {hero}. We can't keep doing this every night.",
"quest.h9.turnin.1": "I kept waiting for the singing to start again. It's really over? Thank you, {hero}. I'll tell the village who we owe for it.",
"quest.b1.offer.1": "Corwin's letting me stay. I sweep, mostly. Four hundred and twelve stairs gives you time to think.",
"quest.b1.offer.2": "I know the Choir's camps. I can show you where they hide. Will you come with me? I don't trust myself to go alone.",
"quest.b1.turnin.1": "I knew some of those men. I thought that would make it easier to face them. It didn't. Thank you for coming.",
"quest.b2.offer.1": "Ansel gave us names. Every brigand he knew who took bone coin. We got more out of him over soup than we did by questioning him.",
"quest.b2.offer.2": "Here's the list. Deal with eight. We'll see how keen the rest are to keep taking Choir work.",
"quest.b2.turnin.1": "Your payment, and a letter of thanks from the Watch. Signed and stamped. Keep it; it may open a few doors.",
"quest.b3.offer.1": "I put three ward stones around the tower the year I left him. They've kept his people out for most of my life.",
"quest.b3.offer.2": "They've gone dark. Touch each one to wake it. I've given you leave to use them. Don't make me regret that.",
"quest.b3.turnin.1": "I can feel them again. Good. Let the Choir try the doorstep now.",
"quest.b4.offer.1": "His apprentice. I'd wondered how he knew so much. I should have asked him years ago.",
"quest.b4.offer.2": "Look for a field journal at the tower. I need to know what he did during the war. All of it.",
"quest.b4.turnin.1": "He held the lantern. Then he went to the Four and told them everything. Seventeen years old, walking out of the Gravelord's camp alone.",
"quest.b4.turnin.2": "This doesn't erase what he did. But I understand why he won't speak of it. I'll return the journal myself.",
"quest.t1.offer.1": "The harpies behind the tower have found my washing line. Forty right socks. That's what they've left me with.",
"quest.t1.offer.2": "Clear the nests off the crag. I'm tired of drying my clothes over the stove.",
"quest.t1.turnin.1": "Good. Hand me that basket, would you, {hero}? I've a month's washing to hang.",
"quest.t2.offer.1": "Their matriarch, Shrieka, has my telescope. She took it while I was looking through it.",
"quest.t2.offer.2": "I need it back. It's how I watch the Choir's camps without giving them the pleasure of watching me.",
"quest.t2.turnin.1": "Lens isn't cracked. Mount's intact. She's cleaned it, too. Hmph.",
"quest.t3.offer.1": "Gristlebones is walking in the Waste again. A giant made from other giants. He used to guard the Gravelord's door.",
"quest.t3.offer.2": "The wards should have kept him down. Destroy him before he reaches anything that matters.",
"quest.t3.turnin.1": "Good. We trapped him on a stairwell last time. Took most of the stairwell with him.",
"quest.g1.offer.1": "The wasps took my shovel. I saw them do it. I'd put it down for a moment and they just... carried it off.",
"quest.g1.offer.2": "Their nests are in the north fields. Could you get her back? The handle's worn to fit my hands. The others aren't the same.",
"quest.g1.turnin.1": "There she is! What's all this sticky stuff? Never mind, it'll wash. Thank you.",
"quest.g2.offer.1": "Some headstones fell when the graves opened. Will you help me set them up?",
"quest.g2.offer.2": "I tried the first one and hurt my back. I don't want the families seeing them like this.",
"quest.g2.turnin.1": "Better. At least people can find the right grave again. Thank you.",
"quest.rv1.offer.1": "Yrsa sent you? Take your spear. We'll start with boars.",
"quest.rv1.offer.2": "Six mossbacks in the clearings. Stay off their tusks. They're slow until they charge.",
"quest.rv1.turnin.1": "Six. Good. Tell the Elder you've taken your first hunt.",
"quest.rv2.offer.1": "Our war-beasts lie beneath the old oaks, north-west of here. They died wearing the druids' collars. We buried them with honours. Now someone's digging them up.",
"quest.rv2.offer.2": "Look at the graves and bring me word. Tell me what you find, however bad it is.",
"quest.rv2.turnin.1": "They've taken the bones and left the bronze. So they weren't after valuables. Let me see that pale cloth.",
"quest.rv3.offer.1": "The Pale Choir. Human grave-robbers who sing over their work. They've brought shovels into our woods.",
"quest.rv3.offer.2": "Drive off six of them. Don't stop to listen to the hymns.",
"quest.rv3.turnin.1": "Good. We'll post a watch at the graves. I won't trust them to stay away.",
"quest.kg1.offer.1": "Newly cracked? Take a moment. The noise is a lot at first. No hurry.",
"quest.kg1.offer.2": "When you're ready, try the cinderlings on the Steps. Old forge sparks. Put out six before they start another fire. Hit through them; there's little weight there.",
"quest.kg1.turnin.1": "Good arm. Now go see the Forge-Mother. She asked me to send you when you were ready.",
"quest.kg2.offer.1": "A thousand golems still lie in the field west of here. The elementalists left them cooling after the war. Some may wake as we did. Perhaps more of our people are in there.",
"quest.kg2.offer.2": "Three stood up last night. Go and see them, little stone. Be careful until you know they're awake.",
"quest.kg2.turnin.1": "Bone sigils? And nothing in their eyes? Someone's taken control of the bodies. They haven't woken at all.",
"quest.kg3.offer.1": "They're heading for Cinderhall. Six rustgolems. Stop them before they get here.",
"quest.kg3.offer.2": "There's no one awake inside them. You saw that yourself. I need to remember it too.",
"quest.kg3.turnin.1": "Thank you. Now we find whoever marked their chests.",
"quest.hs1.offer.1": "You're awake. Give your eyes a moment. It feels strange at first. Can you hear me clearly?",
"quest.hs1.offer.2": "We need help on the fen paths. Bogwights are putting out the lamps, and people get lost without them. Drive off six, if you're ready.",
"quest.hs1.turnin.1": "The lamps are safe. Thank you. Mother Noll will want to see you. She looks after the newly woken.",
"quest.hs2.offer.1": "Three more went last night. Straight out of bed, barefoot. Eyes shut. The tracks follow the old causeway west.",
"quest.hs2.offer.2": "See where they went. Stay within reach of the lamps, love.",
"quest.hs2.turnin.1": "Past the lamps, toward the old camp? The Thrall-Pits. That's where they kept us. Why would anyone go back?",
"quest.hs3.offer.1": "We tried to bring them home. They attacked us. Their eyes had gone dark. We call them the Lost now.",
"quest.hs3.offer.2": "Put six to rest if you find them. I wish I could ask you for something else.",
"quest.hs3.turnin.1 [wend]": "I'll mark six lamps. 'Lost,' under 'Unknown.' We never learned their names.",
"quest.c1.offer.1": "Quell, harbormaster. Welcome to Saltmarrow. I'd give you the tour, but the fishmongers are about to stop work.",
"quest.c1.offer.2": "Shore crabs got into the barrels again. Clear ten off the quay. Watch your feet when you lift the lids.",
"quest.c1.turnin.1": "Fishmongers are back at work. Here's your pay. Buy something before the prices go up again.",
"quest.c2.offer.1": "Redwake's crews are charging boats to land. They've put camps along the shore to enforce it. This is a free port. They don't get to do that.",
"quest.c2.offer.2": "Take out twelve corsairs or the smugglers backing them. Break their hold on the beaches.",
"quest.c2.turnin.1": "Boats are landing without paying him. Good. Now we wait for Redwake to show himself.",
"quest.c3.offer.1": "Redwake hides in the north camp. Cut down enough of his crew and he'll come out. Be ready when he does.",
"quest.c3.offer.2": "Bring me his hat as proof. Feather and all.",
"quest.c3.turnin.1": "That's his. Gods, it's even bigger up close. Here's the bounty. The hat stays with me.",
"quest.c4.offer.1": "Tessaly. I buy information. Sometimes I need someone to fetch it. You look available.",
"quest.c5.offer.1": "Mother Brine owes me money. She runs the sea caves under the Rock, which makes visiting her rather inconvenient.",
"quest.c5.offer.2": "Take a group and collect. She'll fight you for it. She always does.",
"quest.c5.turnin.1": "Settled, then. Thank you. I'll have to find someone else for the brandy.",
"quest.c8.offer.1": "There's a squall on Smuggler's Rock that moves as if it knows where our ships are. The men call it the Tidecaller. You'll find it at the peak.",
"quest.c8.offer.2": "Kill it and the lesser storms should scatter. Take a group. It won't let you climb unchallenged.",
"quest.c8.turnin.1": "We can see blue sky over the Rock. I'll get the patrols moving. Thank you, from all of Halyard.",
"quest.c12.offer.1": "The war fleet lies off the reef north-east of Halyard Isle. Its crews are moving again, still carrying the weapons they drowned with.",
"quest.c12.offer.2": "Clear twelve. Take a Bard if you can; you'll be underwater for most of it.",
"quest.c12.turnin.1": "Twelve down. Good. Catch your breath. There's something else under that reef, and I need to ask for your help.",
"quest.dd2.offer.1": "Crawlers are ambushing caravans on the Lowmarket roads. Clear fourteen of them. The traders won't risk another crossing until we do.",
"quest.dd2.turnin.1": "First caravan's through. I'll keep patrols on the road while they unload.",
"quest.dd3.offer.1": "Scout the Fungal Reach to the west. The growth is spreading toward us, and the mushrooms share a mind. I need to know how far it's reached. Take your report south to Kettle at Deepwatch.",
"quest.dd3.turnin.1 [kettle]": "Gold spores? That means Mycelius is awake. The whole Reach is part of it. We've seen Hollowborn taking food in there.",
"quest.dd3.turnin.2 [kettle]": "You're at Deepwatch now. Last fort before the Lamp. Wipe those spores off before you touch anything.",
"quest.dd4.offer.1": "Hollowborn in the Warrens, west of here. They come up every night carrying water to drown the Lamp. We've held them off so far.",
"quest.dd4.offer.2": "Push them back. Twelve should buy us some breathing room.",
"quest.dd4.turnin.1": "That'll slow them down. I'll put another watch on the road in case it doesn't.",
"quest.dd5.offer.1": "Faceless things come up the Starless Steps whenever the Lamp flickers. They leave black shards when they die.",
"quest.dd5.offer.2": "Bring me six. I have a suspicion, but I need to hold one before I can be sure.",
"quest.dd5.turnin.1": "This is older than sunlight. Solid night. They came from behind the door. There's already a way through.",
"quest.dd6.offer.1": "Saal leads the Hollowborn. His temple's under the Warrens. He's taught them how to put out our lamps, and he's opening the door.",
"quest.dd6.offer.2": "Take a full group. He's been preparing that temple for ten years.",
"quest.dd6.turnin.1": "The Lamp's steady. First time in a month I haven't had to watch it flicker. You killed him, then. Thank you.",
"quest.dd7.offer.1": "Saal was looking for the Vault of Echoes, down the Starless Steps. Every word spoken down here is supposed to linger there. He wanted the last words said before the door was sealed.",
"quest.dd7.offer.2": "Whatever's behind that door wants them too. Find the oldest echo and silence it.",
"quest.dd7.turnin.1": "Vhorun. Sorrel recognised it; you should have seen his face. At least we have a name for Hesper's One Beneath now.",
"quest.dd8.offer.1": "There's a vault at the bottom of the Starless Steps. That's where the door is. The Hollowborn have something guarding it, a Herald. It speaks for Vhorun, and it's working on the lock.",
"quest.dd8.offer.2": "You'll need a raid. Bring everyone you can. I'll keep the Lamp burning for your return.",
"quest.dd8.turnin.1": "The door's shut. We've checked. I don't know how long it'll hold, but your people can rest tonight. Thank you, Lightkeeper.",
"quest.dq1.offer.1": "Mycelius has taken the Court in the Fungal Reach. The mushrooms there are taller than houses. Every root you see belongs to it.",
"quest.dq1.turnin.1": "Spores have settled. We can breathe in the Reach again.",
"quest.dq2.offer.1": "Obb bought the Drowned Mines. Seller said there were a few problems. Monster, dead foreman, ceiling that walks. Obb should have asked which problems.",
"quest.dq2.offer.2": "Clear them out. Obb will make you a partner. We can discuss percentages afterwards.",
"quest.dq2.turnin.1": "Excellent. Your shares are... you want gold? Now? Obb sees. Here.",
"quest.dds2.offer.1": "Barn-sized grub in the Reach. It swallowed a caravan. Kill it before we lose another.",
"quest.dds2.turnin.1": "I'll let the traders know. We still have crawlers out there, but at least they can see the road now.",
"quest.nn2.offer.1": "The beasts around Hearthfrost are starving. We can't reach the woodpile safely. Kill fourteen so the woodcutters can get back to work.",
"quest.nn2.turnin.1": "I'll send the woodcutters out. Stay by the fire a while. You've earned a warm seat.",
"quest.nn4.offer.1": "Kaldmark's army froze on that field a hundred years ago. Now the soldiers are walking. Put twelve down. Look at their eyes if you can get close enough.",
"quest.nn4.turnin.1": "Blue light. Something's calling them. The Wintersworn have been singing out there; I'd start with them.",
"quest.cc2.offer.1": "The Regent withdrew the field patrols. Now farmers can't reach their own crops without being attacked. Clear fourteen beasts from the King's Fields. The city needs that grain.",
"quest.cc3.offer.1": "Find Pennant Grey in Corrandel. The Regent dismissed him as spymaster. That hasn't stopped him working. He'll know who intercepted my letters.",
"quest.cc3.turnin.1 [pennant]": "Carrow sent you. His letters reached the Duke of Ash. The Duke burned them on the Regent's orders.",
"quest.cc3.turnin.2 [pennant]": "He needs to know something else. The Regent used to lead the Pale Choir. Their Choir-Mother is running his kingdom.",
"quest.cc4.offer.1": "The Crown did sell Thornfield's land to the Choir. The rebels have every reason to be angry. Unfortunately, they're burning food wagons on the south road.",
"quest.cc4.offer.2": "Break up twelve of them. We need that road open. Perhaps then Lord Thornfield will talk.",
"quest.cc4.turnin.1": "The attacks have slowed. Edric still refuses to parley. Says he'll only listen to someone who can beat him.",
"quest.yss1.offer.1": "Ammara calls this the Stormreach. The Halcyon's outer defences. We've got Gale's Rest, at least.",
"quest.yss1.offer.2": "Clear twelve creatures from the nearby isles. The builders can't work with griffons and sharks coming at them.",
"quest.yss1.turnin.1": "Tamsin's got the railing going up. We'll finally have something to stop people walking off the edge.",
"quest.yws1.offer.1": "Seventeen Wardens up the lift. We've taken Thunderhead Watch. Clear twelve creatures around the Thunderheads so we can hold it.",
"quest.yws1.turnin.1": "The watch is secure. I'll get the next shift settled in. You've done good work.",
"quest.yss2.offer.1": "Halcyon soldiers wear their names on seals. In case they forget. The hollowed still have them, though they can't read their own names any more.",
"quest.yss2.offer.2": "Bring me six. I may know some of them.",
"quest.yss2.turnin.1": "Corwen. Lissa. Tamar. Brannoc... he used to bring me honey cakes. Elys. Thorn. Leave these with me, please.",
"quest.ycs1.turnin.1 [lirael]": "You crossed the cloud-bridge? Come inside. How many of you made it?",
"quest.ycs2.offer.1": "The Empress had glass guardians grown to patrol the Shelf. No one's tending them now, and they're attacking anything that moves. Clear fourteen from the Prism Fields to open our road.",
"quest.ycs2.turnin.1": "The road's clear. My people saw you fighting out there. They've stopped asking whether we can trust you.",
"quest.ycs3.offer.1": "When the Starwrights arrived, the Magistrate collected every name in Lower Halcyon. People queued to give them. An official register, he said. For the guests.",
"quest.ycs3.offer.2": "Venn's still in the city, taking names. Stop him.",
"quest.ycs3.turnin.1": "You've burned the register? Good. They won't get anyone else from that list.",
"quest.yrs1.turnin.1 [astrin]": "Someone made it. Good. Sit here; I'll show you what I've been watching.",
"quest.yrs2.offer.1": "The Starsworn volunteered their names. They worship the Starwrights. Twelve of them are guarding the Lens-Fields, keeping the rest of us from seeing what's coming. Get them out of the way.",
"quest.yrs2.turnin.1": "Look through here. That bright point. Keep watching. See how it moves?",
"quest.yrs3.turnin.1": "The Great Lens is broken? Then they can't watch the ground. We've bought ourselves time.",
"quest.xw1.offer.1": "Welcome to Lampfall. Mira said to expect you. She means to follow as soon as she's able.",
"quest.xw1.offer.2": "Things from the deep followed Vhorun out. Clear twelve between camp and the rim. My men need room to build a wall.",
"quest.xw1.turnin.1": "Wall's up. It won't stop him, but it'll keep the smaller things off us while we sleep.",
"quest.xw2.offer.1": "There's light trapped in the scales he shed. Candles, hearth fires. I've seen eyes in one.",
"quest.xw2.offer.2": "The creatures below are eating them. Bring me six scales before they're gone. I want to see if the lights are still alive.",
"quest.xw2.turnin.1": "A cooking fire in this one. See the pot above it? That's a lighthouse beam in the next. This little blue one... a nightlight, perhaps.",
"quest.xw2.turnin.2": "He swallowed all of these and kept eating. I don't think he can feel full, Lightkeeper.",
"quest.xw3.offer.2": "Brask's in there. He looked at Vhorun. They all did. Put them to rest, and deal with that walking foundation stone. I can't send my people back in there.",
"quest.xw3.turnin.1": "Did Brask know you were there? No. Leave it. I'll speak to Mira about a candle.",
"quest.xm1.offer.2": "Clear twelve from the Candle Road. That's our food route. We can't afford to lose the carts.",
"quest.xm1.turnin.1": "Nell has someone ready to relight the road. Eleven years old, and he volunteered before anyone asked. I hate having to send him.",
"quest.xm2.offer.1": "The beasts are fat. I can render that into tallow. Yes, those beasts. It'll burn.",
"quest.xm2.offer.2": "Bring eight lumps. I can make four hundred candles from that. Enough for a whole street tonight.",
"quest.xm2.turnin.1": "Put it by the vat. Phew. Open the door on your way out, would you? This will take a while.",
"quest.xm3.offer.1": "Ninety thousand people lived in Avenmoor. When the dark reached them, they sat down wherever they were. After a while they got up. They'd changed.",
"quest.xm3.offer.2": "Aldric's still issuing orders from the town hall. We need him stopped.",
"quest.xm3.turnin.1": "I used to play cards with Aldric. Sorry. Did he say anything about the King?",
"quest.xm3.turnin.2": "The cathedral. Aldwin went there whenever he wanted to be left alone. We should have looked there first.",
"quest.xf1.offer.1": "South, is it? Keep your hands covered. This cold will take a finger before you notice.",
"quest.xf1.offer.2": "Ulvhar's back. The ice advances a mile a week, and hungry creatures come with it. Clear twelve around the Thaw. Then we can talk.",
"quest.xf1.turnin.1": "You're asking about the Tithe Road? Who are you looking for?",
"quest.xf1.turnin.2": "Your {rel}. Speak to Hallvard at Hearth's End. He escaped the cells. If anyone remembers, he will.",
"quest.xf2.offer.1": "Your {rel} had cell nine when I escaped. The night before, {she} gave me {her} bread. Said I'd need it for the run.",
"quest.xf2.offer.2": "The tithe-takers carry numbered prisoner tokens. Bring six. If nine's still in use, we have somewhere to start.",
"quest.xf2.turnin.2": "Nine. They haven't crossed it out. They cross out the dead. There's still someone in that cell.",
"quest.xt1.offer.1": "My hands have stopped shaking. Somewhere in the March, I noticed I could hold a lamp steady again.",
"quest.xt1.offer.2": "He's lying in the Throat of the World, feeding. The things around him live on the scraps. Clear twelve so we can light the camp's last lamp without drawing them in.",
"quest.xt1.turnin.1": "There. Last Light. Shield it from the wind while I fix the wick. He can see us from here. Let him.",
"quest.xt2.offer.1": "Ammara. We met in the Stormreach. I escaped before the Starwrights could take my name. I've followed them here. They're watching Vhorun.",
"quest.xt2.offer.2": "They use lenses to see across the dark. Bring me six. I need to see what they're looking for.",
"quest.xt2.turnin.1": "Look through this. He looks different, doesn't he? Small. Frightened. That's how they see him. Their lost child.",
"quest.xt2.turnin.2": "They mean to take him back. Even after all this.",
"quest.xt3.offer.1": "The plain west of camp is covered in his bite marks. Something's living in the largest. The ground opens when you step on it, and you're gone.",
"quest.xt3.offer.2": "My flame's on the other side. Clear a path for me, Lightkeeper. I've come too far to stop here.",
"quest.xt3.turnin.1": "I saw the blue flame while you were fighting. Still moving. Still there. I can reach it now. Thank you.",
"quest.xt4.offer.1": "You can see his ribs from here. The pilgrims who walked into his mouth are still singing inside. A Starwright herald is guarding them.",
"quest.xt4.offer.2": "Stop the singing. It keeps him calm enough for the Starwrights to approach. We can't let them take him yet.",
"quest.xt4.turnin.1": "'A family matter.' That's what the herald told you? They used those words at court, before they took the names. As if the rest of us had no business objecting.",
"quest.xt5.offer.1": "There's a crack in his side. You can climb down to the heart. It beats once a minute. Watch the sky; you'll see the lights dim when it does.",
"quest.xt5.offer.2": "Stop it. That won't kill him, but it should weaken him enough for us to fight.",
"quest.xt5.turnin.1": "The lights went dim. We thought we'd lost you. Then they came back brighter. It worked. We can go after him.",
"quest.xt6.offer.1": "The Compact's here. Corrand's Legion too, and the Candlehold Free and Thawborn. They've brought lanterns. We have enough to light the whole camp.",
"quest.xt6.offer.2": "Your friends are waiting for you. They wouldn't let us leave them behind.",
"quest.xt6.offer.3": "Twenty-four for the descent. Go down the Throat of the World, Lightkeeper. Finish him. We'll hold the way back.",
"quest.xt6.turnin.1 [mira13]": "He's dead. Look up. Look at the sky.",
"quest.xt7.offer.1 [mira13]": "They came an hour after he fell. Seven Starwrights. Walked straight past us. I had my weapon out. They never looked at it.",
"quest.xt7.offer.2 [ammara]": "They left the body. Whatever hunger survived in him, they gathered it into a vessel. Like a lantern. It went dark as they sealed it. Then they rose out of sight.",
"quest.xt7.offer.3 [mira13]": "Ammara thinks they'll bring it back. Long after we're gone, perhaps. I wish they'd left us anything else to remember them by.",
"quest.xt7.turnin.1 [mira13]": "I'm going back to Deepwatch. Sela's glass should let us rebuild the Lamp. There's a lot to do.",
"quest.xt7.turnin.2 [mira13]": "Come and see it when it's lit. I'd like you there. Thank you, Lightkeeper. For getting us home.",
"quest.xtx1.offer.1": "Greedmaw's on the plain. It's eaten enough of Vhorun's scraps to start looking like him. Now it's taken our second ember. Please kill it.",
"quest.xtx1.turnin.1": "Good. I'll say a prayer. After I've checked the ember.",
"quest.xtx2.offer.1": "His scavengers have swallowed lights from the scraps. Candles, sparks, whole lighthouses. Free eight. You'll see them rise once they're loose.",
"quest.xtx2.turnin.1": "Watch that little one. There it goes. I wonder whose window it'll end up in.",
"quest.xty1.offer.1": "I need a relief watch at the ember. Clear twelve creatures so I can get some sleep.",
"quest.xty1.turnin.1": "Still burning. Thank you. Wake me if they come back.",
"quest.xty2.offer.1": "They're coming for the lamp again. Kill ten before they reach it.",
"quest.xty2.turnin.1": "Wick's holding. Oil's good. We'll manage another night.",
"talk.warden.bio": "Ilse has kept the Watch running in {town} for eleven years. Her desk is buried in reports. She knows which one you're here about.",
"talk.warden.greet.1": "Morning, {hero}. Trouble, or work?",
"talk.warden.greet.2": "Good, you're back. What did you find?",
"talk.warden.topic1.answer.1": "Joined at sixteen. Kept seeing things nobody would do anything about. Thought a uniform might help. It did, sometimes. I've been at it eleven years now.",
"talk.warden.topic2.answer.1": "The wolves are taking sheep, the brigands are stopping wagons, and Wick's reported empty graves. Pick a direction. I could use help in all of them.",
"talk.warden.topic3.answer.1": "He turns up. Frightened out of his wits, usually, but he turns up. I've had guards who couldn't manage that. Don't tell him I said so.",
"talk.tanner.bio": "Bram has worked leather in {town} for decades. He keeps working the hide across his knee while he talks, pausing to inspect your boots.",
"talk.tanner.greet.1": "Buying, selling, or just escaping the weather?",
"talk.tanner.greet.2": "Careful of the racks. That lot's still drying.",
"talk.tanner.topic1.answer.1": "Plenty of work. Not enough leather. The orcs keep hunters out of the wood, and the brigands keep merchants off the road. Can't make boots out of promises.",
"talk.tanner.topic2.answer.1": "Orcs hold most of it. {tusk} has the hollow at the far end. I've lost good hunters to {tusk}. Stay out of that hollow.",
"talk.sister.bio": "Maren tends the temple of the Four. She keeps a copy of the Law on her desk, beside the names of people who need visiting.",
"talk.sister.greet.2": "Sit down. You can tell me when you've caught your breath.",
"talk.sister.topic1.answer.2": "Eight kings signed. Four summoners witnessed. A hundred years without another war like that is worth defending.",
"talk.sister.topic2.answer.2": "They were people before we made them holy. Frightened people, some of them. I find that comforting.",
"talk.sister.topic3.answer.2": "No one seems able to tell me where they buried him.",
"talk.quell.bio": "Quell keeps Saltmarrow's harbour moving and its ledger within reach. Anyone proposing royal oversight gets the same answer.",
"talk.quell.greet.1": "Off the ropes, please. Yes, you. Welcome to Saltmarrow.",
"talk.quell.greet.2": "Back from the Vale? Come through. What's happened?",
"talk.quell.topic1.answer.1": "Free port. You land, you trade, you leave. No king gets to decide who docks here. It brings us some rotten company, but I'll take that over a royal customs office.",
"talk.quell.topic2.answer.1": "The ferry runs a circuit: Saltmarrow, Fort Halyard, Smuggler's Rock, Gullwick. Miss it and you can rent a rowboat at any dock for two gold. Swimming's possible. So are sharks. Watch your breath if you try it.",
"talk.tessaly.bio": "Tessaly closes her ledger when you approach, keeping a finger between the pages.",
"talk.tessaly.greet.1": "There you are. Sit. I'd like to hear your version.",
"talk.tessaly.greet.2": "Is this a purchase, or a confidence?",
"talk.tessaly.topic1.answer.1": "People tell me things. I pay them. Then someone else pays me rather more. Were you hoping to buy or sell?",
"talk.steward.greet.1": "House, plot, or furniture? I can show you what's available.",
"talk.steward.greet.2": "Have a seat. That one's for sale, if you like it.",
"talk.ashby.bio": "Commodore Ashby commands Fort Halyard with fewer marines than the coast needs. The empty spaces on the duty roster bother Ashby more than the enemy reports.",
"talk.ashby.greet.2": "Good. Another fighter. Are you available?",
"talk.ashby.topic1.answer.1": "The necromancers lost a whole fleet off the north-east reef a hundred years ago. Every crew went down with it. Now we're seeing those crews on the beaches.",
"talk.wenna.bio": "Wenna mends Gullwick's nets with quick, swollen fingers. When someone mentions a missing boat, she stops to listen.",
"talk.wenna.greet.1": "Step over the net, love. I've just mended that bit.",
"talk.wenna.topic1.answer.1": "We fish. Some days there's enough to sell, some days enough to eat. You've seen the empty boats on the shore? I knew the men who worked them.",
"talk.wick.bio": "The gravedigger of {town} keeps three lanterns within reach. His hands settle when he picks up a shovel; put him in front of a stranger and he starts fidgeting again.",
"talk.wick.greet.1": "Oh, it's you. Sorry. I heard footsteps and... hello.",
"talk.wick.greet.2": "I've moved into the tool shed. Better view of the graves. Worse bed.",
"talk.wick.topic1.answer.1": "Uncle Bartholomew did it. His father before him. I wanted to bake, but when Uncle died, someone had to bury him. Then someone else died, and I still had the shovel.",
"talk.wick.topic2.answer.1": "Haven't had much sleep. I keep thinking I hear digging. Could you stay a minute?",
"talk.wick.topic3.answer.1": "Never seen the sea. I've got my shovels, a lantern, and this hat. The man in the shop said it was nautical. Does it look nautical to you?",
"talk.pell.bio": "Dobbin Pell has spent twenty-two years making promises on behalf of Little Hollin. Most of his current correspondence begins with an apology.",
"talk.pell.greet.1": "Come in! Mrs. Gubbins is in the parlour. Best leave the furniture where she's put it.",
"talk.pell.greet.2": "{hero}! Stay for a meal, won't you? I'll find something.",
"talk.pell.topic1.answer.1": "Forty-two of us. Two hundred sheep. Excellent turnips, when the boar leaves us any. It's a good place to live. Usually. I know you haven't seen us at our best.",
"talk.pell.topic2.answer.1": "Our schoolteacher. Fifty years she taught here. That's why nobody argues when she moves a chair. You never quite stop being frightened of your old teacher, do you?",
"talk.wenlow.bio": "Wenlow's doorway is hung with charm bags. Inside, she has herbs drying above the stove and very little patience for interruptions.",
"talk.wenlow.greet.2": "Shut the door. What do you need?",
"talk.wenlow.topic1.answer.1": "Sage, salt, spider silk. Sew it tight and hang it over the window. If the stitching breaks, bring it back. Don't try to mend it with ordinary thread.",
"talk.wenlow.topic2.answer.1": "I delivered Dobbin Pell. Loud baby. Hasn't improved much.",
"talk.haskett.bio": "You can see the millstones through Haskett's chest. He notices you looking and moves aside so you can inspect them properly.",
"talk.haskett.greet.1": "Fresh flour! Have a look. Don't blow on it.",
"talk.haskett.greet.2": "Keep your sleeves clear of the stones. They're solid, even if I'm not.",
"talk.haskett.topic1.answer.1": "I miss meals. Didn't think I would, but I do. Otherwise the work's much the same. No aching back, at least. Still get people wanting credit.",
"talk.haskett.topic2.answer.1": "Went out after that boar. It was in my turnips again. Next thing I remember, I could see through my own hand. Turnips were gone too. Bloody waste of a Tuesday.",
"talk.ansel.bio": "Ansel has stopped wearing the Choir's robes. He still catches himself humming, then goes quiet.",
"talk.ansel.greet.1": "Corwin's given me work. It helps having something to do.",
"talk.ansel.greet.2": "I've nearly finished the stairs. You can get through if you keep to the dry side.",
"talk.ansel.topic1.answer.1": "Tobin drowned in the millpond when we were boys. They said I could bring him back. I believed them. Every time I doubted, I thought: what if I stop now, and tonight would have been the night?",
"talk.ansel.topic2.answer.1": "I'm going to visit his grave. I've never been. That sounds awful, doesn't it? I couldn't make myself go. After that, whatever work needs doing.",
"talk.corwin.bio": "Corwin has spent a century in this tower, refusing to discuss the war. He keeps the door locked and the windows where he can see them.",
"talk.corwin.greet.1": "The door, please. I'm heating the room, not the Waste.",
"talk.corwin.greet.2": "Stool's free. Leave the chair alone.",
"talk.corwin.topic1.answer.1": "Old magic. Some of it mine. That's all you're getting.",
"talk.corwin.topic2.answer.1": "Loud. You couldn't hear orders half the time. Just stood there waiting for someone to point. I remember the smell. I remember thinking the officers looked old. Most of them were younger than you.",
"talk.corwin.topic3.answer.1": "Brilliant. You'd ask him a question and forget to be frightened while he answered. He spoke to the dead as if they were guests. Said raising them was a kindness.",
"talk.corwin.topic3.answer.2": "I believed him, {hero}. That's the part I can't get past.",
"talk.banker.greet.1": "Making a deposit, or taking something out?",
"talk.banker.topic1.answer.1": "Same vault for every class you play. Store a sword as a Bulwark and it'll still be here when you return as an Elementalist.",
"talk.armorer.greet.1": "Looking for a weapon? Let me see how you hold the one you've got.",
"talk.armorer.greet.2": "Back for training? Clear some space by the rack.",
"talk.dace.greet.1": "Crouch. Their crossbows reach this part of the road.",
"talk.dace.greet.2": "Tell me you're here about the keep.",
"talk.dace.topic1.answer.1": "Smuggler. Now he calls himself the Bandit King. Started buying men and stonework when someone began paying him for corpses. That's where his crown came from.",
"talk.dace.topic2.answer.1": "We haven't caught the buyer. The carts go east at night, toward the Waste. Pale Choir would be my guess.",
"talk.fenna.greet.2": "Something's wrong with the wood. Even the roots feel wrong.",
"talk.fenna.topic1.answer.1": "Syra came back in spring. Grey robes. Singing to the trees. Everything around her rotted, then started moving.",
"talk.fenna.topic1.answer.2": "She was a druid here once. Walked these paths with me. Now she looks at all this and tells me it's growing.",
"talk.fest_midsummer.bio": "Penhallow keeps the Midsummer Fair moving with a bell and a list of stalls. The list is sticky with cake icing.",
"talk.fest_dead.bio": "Osk has set out more places than there are guests. Each empty chair has a candle in front of it.",
"talk.fest_harvest.bio": "Reeve Barleycorn checks the food stores himself before declaring the harvest good. This year, he's letting people take seconds.",
"talk.fest_wintereve.bio": "Mother Hollin keeps a kettle hot through the longest night. She notices when someone arrives without a gift and quietly presses one into their hand.",
"talk.isolde.greet.2": "The Marshal paid for a ship. So far I've got half a hull. We're working on it.",
"talk.oriel.greet.1": "If you're going up the Spire, speak to me first. No one's survived the climb in a century.",
"talk.oriel.greet.2": "Keep your eyes on the stair. Things come down it now.",
"talk.fennick.bio": "Fennick has cleared a space on the bench by pushing several unfinished devices onto the floor. He appears to consider this progress.",
"talk.fennick.greet.1": "Don't touch that lead. I haven't marked the polarity yet.",
"talk.fennick.greet.2": "Got the parts? Put them here. Let me see the old fittings first.",
"talk.tamhale.greet.1": "Away from the edge! Railings go in tomorrow. Until then, hold a rope.",
"talk.tamhale.greet.2": "Forty years waiting to sail again. Have you seen that view?",
"talk.ammara.greet.1": "You're from the ground? Sorry. I've never spoken to anyone from there.",
"talk.ammara.greet.2": "If a Starwright asks your name, don't answer. Please remember that.",
"talk.ammara.topic1.answer.1": "A year ago, they came down from beyond the sky. The Empress received them in her garden. They stayed a month. We thought she was negotiating a treaty.",
"talk.ammara.topic1.answer.2": "They'd lost something they made. It went beneath our world. They offered to lift Halcyon to the stars if we helped them find it.",
"talk.ammara.topic2.answer.1": "They ask your name. It's such a small thing to ask that people answer before they think. Then they can't remember what they said.",
"talk.ammara.topic2.answer.2": "The sailors still obey orders. Still fight. But try asking one about home. There's nothing left to answer you.",
"talk.lirael.greet.1": "Ground-folk. Welcome to Prismhold. Yes, I mean it. Things have changed.",
"talk.lirael.greet.2": "We haven't given up Halcyon. We left the Empress. There's a difference.",
"talk.lirael.topic1.answer.1": "No children in twenty years. The cloudstone's doing something to us. We've lived up here a thousand years, and now we're dying out. The Empress has buried everyone she loved.",
"talk.lirael.topic1.answer.2": "They promised her a way out. Take us to the stars, let us live forever. She wanted it too badly to ask what they'd take in return.",
"talk.astrin.greet.1": "You beat my father at the Spire. I know why you had to. Give me a little time before we talk about it.",
"talk.astrin.greet.2": "Eleven notebooks. If you want to know about the Starwrights, start with this one.",
"talk.astrin.topic1.answer.1": "They make living things. Before our world had a name, they made something to consume the dark between stars. They wanted their worlds lit forever.",
"talk.astrin.topic1.answer.2": "It kept eating. Grew until it fell through the sky and buried itself beneath our world. They lost track of it there. Vhorun. The name means something like 'the one we made too hungry'.",
"talk.astrin.topic2.answer.1": "They call him their child. They want him back. I asked what happens to us when they recover him. I couldn't make them understand why that mattered.",
"talk.astrin.topic2.answer.2": "Ithrel came ahead to find him. The others are waiting for the signal to use the Gate.",
"talk.jack12.topic1.answer.1": "Kept changing jobs. Usually just after someone told me to leave. But I learned the basics, and I remember where I went wrong. Useful things to know when you're teaching.",
"scene.intro.1": "The summoners fought their war with whatever they could bind. Druids sent beasts into battle. Elementalists marched behind fire and storm. The necromancers raised the fallen and sent them back.",
"scene.intro.2": "A hundred years ago, the survivors signed the Fourfold Law. The dead would rest. No summoner could bind more than four creatures. The war ruins would stay sealed, and what had been bound would go free.",
"scene.intro.3": "In {town}, someone has started opening graves.",
"scene.intro.4 [wick]": "Hello? Say something. Anything. I need to know you're alive.",
"scene.drag.1": "Two furrows cut through the long grass. You follow them north, past the last field.",
"scene.drag.2": "Beyond lies the Ossuary. The necromancers built it from bone during the war. No one in the Vale has entered it in a hundred years.",
"scene.hollin.1": "Sheep crop the grass outside Little Hollin. Beside the well, a man reaches for the bucket. His hand passes through it. He tries again.",
"scene.hollin.2 [pell]": "Visitors! Welcome! That one won't trouble you. Keep away from the fence, though. Yes, over here. Quickly.",
"scene.apprentice.1 [corwin]": "I was seventeen. He asked me to hold a lantern while he worked. I stood there watching him stitch men together. I knew what I was looking at. I held it steady anyway.",
"scene.apprentice.2 [corwin]": "I was his apprentice, {hero}. When I left, I went to the Four. Told them everything I knew, including how to kill him.",
"scene.apprentice.3 [corwin]": "I thought they'd done it.",
"scene.gravelord.1": "Grathul hits the floor. Frost spreads across the altar, and green light gathers above it. A man's face takes shape.",
"scene.gravelord.2 [gravelord]": "Eleven years of work. Look at what you've done to him.",
"scene.gravelord.3 [gravelord]": "Keep the bones, then. The Vale can have its graveyard back. There are fleets beneath the Saltreach. I won't need to stitch those crews together.",
"scene.gravelord.4 [gravelord]": "Tell Corwin his room is ready. He'll know what I mean.",
"scene.intro_varr.1": "The war-beasts were bred to obey. Wolves learned to hold spears. Stags carried soldiers. When the summoner wars ended, the druids left them behind.",
"scene.intro_varr.2": "The beasts made homes of their own. They learned to speak, build, and bury their dead. They named themselves Varr: the unleashed.",
"scene.intro_varr.3": "This spring, someone began digging up their war graves in the Ironbark Weald.",
"scene.intro_grael.1": "The elementalists gave their war golems hearts of living fire. After the war, they left them in the Kilnlands to cool.",
"scene.intro_grael.2": "The stone cooled within a year. The hearts took a century. As the hearts cooled, the stone cracked open. The beings inside woke with minds of their own. They call themselves the Grael.",
"scene.intro_grael.3": "Now more bodies are stirring in the Golem Field. The Grael have tried to speak to them. Something is wrong.",
"scene.intro_sallow.1": "When the war ended, the necromancers released their dead. The bodies should have fallen where they stood.",
"scene.intro_sallow.2": "Instead, some woke. They could think, speak, and choose, though none remembered who they had been. They call themselves the Sallow. Most kingdoms refuse to recognise them as people.",
"scene.intro_sallow.3": "This month, a voice began singing in the Hushmoor. The Sallow can hear it calling them back to their graves.",
"lore.law.text": "Agreed by the necromancer, druid and elementalist courts, and the eight surviving kingdoms, at the close of the summoner wars.\\nI. The dead shall stay dead.\\nII. No summoner shall bind more than four creatures.\\nIII. The war ruins shall remain sealed.\\nIV. Whatever was bound in war shall be set free in peace.\\nEight kings signed below. Four summoners witnessed.",
"lore.ledger.text": "Monday: Two graves dug.\\nTuesday: Both filled.\\nWednesday: Abernathy's open. Filled it again.\\nThursday: Open again. Packed the dirt down properly this time.\\nFriday: Footprints. Outward. Bought another lantern.\\nSaturday: Bought another lantern.",
"lore.hymn.text": "Rise, O sleepers, leave the clay;\\nYour lord has need of you today.\\nThe kings may seal your graves with stone;\\nTheir law can neither hold nor own.\\nA note beside the last verse: 'Wait for the bell. Last time you came in early.'",
"lore.register.text": "Births: 2. Deaths: 3. Returned: 41.\\nBrother Ansel requests use of the chapel bell. Approved, D. Pell.\\nBelow, in the same hand: Revoke approval. Find Ansel.",
"lore.journal.text": "Ninth siege, spring. He used the men from the north wall. I recognised one by the scar on his hand. The master called the thing beautiful and asked me to bring the lantern closer. I did.\\nI have packed what I can carry. Tomorrow I go to the Four. If they hang me after I tell them, at least they'll know.",
"lore.letter.text": "Deacon,\\nSend only what Grathul needs to the Ossuary. The rest go east. Three fleets lie beneath the Saltreach, and I want crews ready when I raise them.\\nLeave Corwin alone. His room is waiting.\\nHave the Choir practise the fourth verse. They keep losing time.",
"lore.wreckledger.text": "Ships wrecked: 9. Sailors: 61.\\nHierophant's payment: 61 crowns. Deduction: 3 crowns. Three reached shore alive; finished with oars.\\nNew instruction: bodies must be whole. No oars.",
"lore.patron.text": "After the Gravelord fell, his mouth moved again. The voice was unfamiliar.\\n'You have killed my herald. The dead of eight kingdoms were promised to me. That debt remains. I am Vhorun. When the last lamp falls, you will see me.'\\nThe green light left his eyes.",
"lore.starwrightnote.text": "Specimen 412. Vhorun.\\nGrowth exceeded projections. Feeding continues beyond required intake. Recovery advised before further damage.\\nA second hand has added: Compare with the other specimens. Do not circulate this report.",
"boss.brask.start": "Shut the gate! Nobody through!",
"boss.moll.start": "Out of my kitchen. Drop the knife first.",
"boss.varro.start": "Keep them whole, lads. The Choir pays by the body.",
"boss.mossgut.start": "Who woke Mossgut?",
"boss.mossgut.half": "Mossgut hungry now.",
"boss.syra.start": "Look at the roots. Even dead, they grow. He was right.",
"boss.ulric.start": "The dead are under my protection. That includes the Choir's.",
"boss.ossuarist.start": "Hold still. You'll splinter them.",
"boss.vess.start": "You should have stopped at Mortlake.",
"boss.grisk.start": "You're late. Get a pick. Get... who let you in?",
"boss.korr.start": "There's another seam below. I know there is. Move!",
"boss.gullet.half": "Stop cutting Gullet!",
"boss.lampjack.start": "Wrong light, friend. You followed the wrong light.",
"boss.saltmother.start": "Boys, strip the valuables first. I'm not fishing coins out of the sea.",
"boss.blackhallow.start": "A crown for each of you. Hold still and I'll earn it quickly.",
"boss.undertow.start": "Hold your breath. It won't help, but you'll try.",
"boss.calloway.start": "Put out the lamps! Let them come ashore!",
"boss.powdernell.start": "Hundred years drying this powder. Don't you dare bleed on it.",
"boss.powdernell.half": "Fuse is lit! MOVE!",
"boss.vey.start": "These ships sail for the master. Clear my dock.",
"boss.oldkingaldous.start": "Who told you Vharos had fallen? Look at me. Your king still stands.",
"boss.mistressanvil.start": "I know that blade. Let's see if you deserve it.",
"boss.forgemasterkael.start": "The Gravelord owes me years yet. You aren't taking them.",
"story.sibling.s1.1": "{friend} hands you a creased letter. Wenna, the younger sister who left to become a sellsword two years ago, wants out of her company. They won't release her.",
"story.sibling.s1.2": "\"I need help getting her out,\" {friend} says. \"I wouldn't ask if I could do it myself.\"",
"story.sibling.s2.1": "Captain Drace holds Wenna's contract. He won't sell it or let her leave. {friend} has tracked the Blackwater Company to a camp nearby.",
"story.sibling.s2.2": "\"Drace is in there,\" {friend} says. \"Once he's down, we get Wenna.\"",
"story.sibling.s3.1": "Wenna is free. She asks to join {friend}'s group, but the answer comes before she's finished. Their mother needs help on the farm. {friend} won't discuss it further.",
"story.sibling.s3.2": "\"Will you talk to her?\" {friend} asks you. \"She thinks I'm trying to keep her a child.\"",
"story.sibling.s4.1": "Wenna's new company took a contract at the edge of the Wound. Half were taken by something from below. Her letter ends mid-sentence, then starts again: \"Please come.\"",
"story.sibling.s4.2": "\"I should have...\" {friend} pulls a strap tight. \"It doesn't matter. We need to go.\"",
"story.sibling.s5.1": "Most of Wenna's company survived. She's starting her own and wants to name it after {friend}.",
"story.sibling.s5.2": "\"She could at least have asked,\" {friend} says, folding the letter carefully enough to save it.",
"story.sibling.choice1": "Urge Wenna to go home. Her family is worried.",
"story.sibling.choice1.result": "{n} watches until Wenna is out of sight. \"She'll be furious with me. I can live with that. Thank you.\"",
"story.sibling.choice2": "Tell Wenna the choice is hers.",
"story.sibling.choice2.result": "Wenna goes to look for another company. {n} turns away when you approach and walks ahead for the next hour.",
"story.rival.s1.1": "Osric Vane is in town. He trained with {friend}, won most of their bouts, and won't let anyone forget it. Now he's telling people {friend} would be dead without you. The story reaches {friend} before evening.",
"story.rival.s1.2": "\"You've saved my life,\" {friend} says. \"I know that. Does everyone think that's all there is to me?\"",
"story.rival.s2.1": "{friend} has agreed to duel Osric outside town. You're {friend}'s second. Osric has brought people who keep their hands on their weapons while the rules are explained.",
"story.rival.s2.2": "\"Watch his friends,\" {friend} says. \"If they move, don't wait for me.\"",
"story.rival.s3.1": "Osric is down. Blood runs into his collar where {friend}'s blade rests against his throat. Someone in the watching crowd calls for you to finish it.",
"story.rival.s3.2": "{friend} glances at you without lowering the blade. \"Well?\"",
"story.rival.s4.1": "Osric went into the March to prove he could outdo {friend}. Now something in his armour hunts the roads. People who knew him won't go near it.",
"story.rival.s4.2": "\"I'd have gone with him if he'd asked,\" {friend} says. \"Come on. We can't leave him like that.\"",
"story.rival.s5.1": "Osric is buried where {friend} wanted, overlooking the country below. The stone still needs an inscription.",
"story.rival.s5.2": "\"He'd correct whatever I put,\" {friend} says. \"Probably tell me I'd spelt his name wrong.\"",
"story.rival.choice1": "Tell them to help Osric up. The duel is over.",
"story.rival.choice1.result": "{n} offers a hand. Osric hesitates, then takes it. \"Next year,\" he says, wiping blood from his mouth. \"We'll see,\" {n} answers, with a reluctant smile.",
"story.rival.choice2": "Let Osric get up on his own.",
"story.rival.choice2.result": "Osric struggles upright to jeers from the crowd. {n} sheathes the blade and asks you to leave with them.",
"story.debt.s1.1": "Mother Grist has called in the debt. {friend} has been making payments since before you met, but the moneylender wants the rest now. She knows where {friend} is staying.",
"story.debt.s1.2": "\"Her collector's called Knuckles,\" {friend} says. \"You'll see why. Try not to let him grab you.\"",
"story.debt.s2.1": "Knuckles and his helpers are waiting on the road. They call for {friend} to come forward. After checking for a way around, {friend} looks at you.",
"story.debt.s2.2": "\"I haven't got the money,\" {friend} says. \"That leaves the other way.\"",
"story.debt.s3.1": "With Knuckles beaten, Mother Grist sends a new bill. The debt, the interest, and the cost of replacing her collector.",
"story.debt.s3.2": "\"That's years,\" {friend} says. \"I could work every day and still... that's years.\"",
"story.debt.s4.1": "Vhorun passed over Mother Grist's counting-house. Now its ledgers collect debts themselves. One has come looking for {friend}.",
"story.debt.s4.2": "\"I know that book,\" {friend} says. \"I used to watch her write in it. Give me something to burn it with.\"",
"story.debt.s5.1": "{friend} waits until the ledger's last page crumbles. No record of the debt remains. You call once, then again, before {friend} steps away from the ashes.",
"story.debt.s5.2": "\"Eleven years,\" {friend} says. \"Every coin I picked up, I knew how much of it was hers. I can keep the next one.\"",
"story.debt.choice1": "Pay off the debt.",
"story.debt.choice1.result": "\"I'll pay you back,\" {n} says. \"I know you aren't asking. Let me say it anyway.\"",
"story.debt.choice2": "Tell Grist she won't be collecting anything else.",
"story.debt.choice2.result": "Mother Grist cancels the debt. {n} reads her reply, then looks at you. \"What exactly did you tell her?\"",
"story.home.s1.1": "A letter from home catches up with {friend}. Something took sheep from the high fields, then started taking shepherds. Four farmers and a dog are all the militia the village has.",
"story.home.s1.2": "\"I said I'd come back if they needed me,\" {friend} says. \"Can we leave now?\"",
"story.home.s2.1": "The hound is as big as a cart. Its eyes catch the light wrong. {friend} keeps watching the fields while the sun drops.",
"story.home.s2.2": "\"The village dog went for it,\" {friend} says. \"Bought them time to run.\"",
"story.home.s3.1": "The village holds a feast for {friend}. Over dinner, the elders ask {friend} to stay and lead the militia. The food goes cold while they wait for an answer.",
"story.home.s3.2": "Outside afterwards, {friend} asks, \"Would you stay? If it were your home?\"",
"story.home.s4.1": "The letter arrived an hour ago. Vhorun's host is at the bridge outside {friend}'s village. Four farmers and a new dog are holding it. {friend} hasn't stopped moving since.",
"story.home.s4.2": "\"Get the hound first,\" {friend} says. \"The rest should scatter once it's down.\"",
"story.home.s5.1": "The village has decided on a statue of {friend}. Someone has chosen a spot in the square. Now a sculptor is asking {friend} to stand still for measurements.",
"story.home.s5.2": "\"Help me,\" {friend} whispers. \"Tell them the dog deserves one. It does.\"",
"story.home.choice1": "Encourage them to stay and help the village.",
"story.home.choice1.result": "{n} returns a week later. \"They had things running by the third day. By the fifth, I was mostly in the way.\" They set down their pack. \"Ready when you are.\"",
"story.home.choice2": "Ask them to stay with you.",
"story.home.choice2.result": "\"You still need me?\" {n} asks. \"All right. I'll speak to the elders before we leave.\"",
"story.past.s1.1": "Old Mother Aedre taught {friend}. She died the winter before you met. Until now, {friend} couldn't face visiting the grave. Last night, {friend} dreamed of her calling and woke in tears.",
"story.past.s1.2": "\"I know a dream doesn't mean anything,\" {friend} says. \"I'd still like to go. Will you come?\"",
"story.past.s2.1": "Aedre's shade paces around the grave. {friend} calls out, but she turns on you both without recognising the voice.",
"story.past.s2.2": "\"Don't hurt her more than you have to,\" {friend} says. \"Please.\"",
"story.past.s3.1": "{friend} stays by the grave after the shade is gone. You wait a little way off. Eventually, you hear footsteps coming toward you.",
"story.past.s3.2": "\"She'd have liked you,\" {friend} says. \"Thank you for waiting.\"",
"story.past.s4.1": "Before she taught, Aedre kept a lantern for the Compact. {friend} has learned it was buried with her. Now something that feeds on lamps has dug it up.",
"story.past.s4.2": "\"She kept it all those years,\" {friend} says. \"We have to get it back.\"",
"story.past.s5.1": "{friend} turns Aedre's battered lantern over, checking the catch. It hasn't burned in twenty years. The glass is still whole. Satisfied, {friend} holds it out to you.",
"story.past.s5.2": "\"Have you got a light?\" {friend} asks. \"I'd like to do this together.\"",
"story.past.choice1": "Tell them you'll come whenever they need you.",
"story.past.choice1.result": "{n} nods and squeezes your arm. You walk back together.",
"story.past.choice2": "Say you're glad you came.",
"story.past.choice2.result": "\"So am I,\" {n} says. \"I nearly didn't ask.\"",
"story.parent.s1.1": "On the first night out of the cells, {friend} sits close to the fire. You hear about the prisoners and the games they made from pebbles. There are gaps in the telling you don't try to fill.",
"story.parent.s1.2": "\"They all knew about you,\" {friend} says. \"Probably could have drawn your face by the end. I talked about you that much.\"",
"story.parent.s2.1": "The Choir has sent Vell to recapture {friend}. Ten years ago, the same hunter took {her} north in chains. Vell will know {friend} on sight.",
"story.parent.s2.2": "\"Vell,\" {friend} says. \"I'd hoped never to hear that name again. Stay close when we find him.\"",
"story.parent.s3.1": "Vell is dead. {friend} keeps watching his hands until you're ready to leave. Then {she} takes a breath and brushes dirt from {her} clothes. \"Does anyone at home know I'm alive?\"",
"story.parent.s3.2": "\"We should write. Unless... do you think we could get there ourselves? Just knock on the door?\"",
"story.parent.s4.1": "{friend} tells you why {she} went after the Choir ten years ago. The Choir-Mother wanted a child from the Vale. You. That was what {she} went to stop. Now the Choir-Mother's shadow has come for you both.",
"story.parent.s4.2": "\"I thought if I kept it from you, you'd be safe,\" {friend} says. \"You should have heard it from me sooner.\"",
"story.parent.s5.1": "With the shadow gone, {friend} sits on the nearest rock. A laugh escapes, then another. Soon {her} face is wet.",
"story.parent.s5.2": "\"I kept thinking she'd come back,\" {friend} says. \"Even when you were winning. Come here, will you? Just for a minute.\"",
"story.parent.choice1.result": "{n} writes for an hour, crosses out half a page, and starts again. The fastest rider in Thawhold takes the finished letter. \"I hope they read it sitting down,\" {n} says.",
"story.parent.choice2.result": "{n} smiles. \"All right. Together. You knock. I'll stand where they can see me.\""
};
